        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "1. Teachers may refer disruptive students to the office from the classroom with a referral slip provided by their principal describing the behavioral problem when, in the judgement of the teacher, normal corrective measures have been ineffective in bringing about satisfactory improvement in the student's behavior. In emergency situations, the student may be sent to the office immediately with a written report to follow.",
            "block_bbox": [
